# SomaMap environment - names only, never values.
#
# Which Supabase project the server talks to is decided by src/lib/supabaseTarget.ts, and the
# rules below are enforced there. The resolver refuses to guess: a configuration that does not
# satisfy them makes sign-in and Delete everything answer "not configured" instead of acting
# on a project nobody chose.
#
# THE HOSTED PAIR - what a deployed build uses. Both halves are required together.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# THE LOCAL PAIR - optional, for running against the stack `supabase start` creates. Both
# halves are required together, and when both pairs are present this pair wins.
#
# The rules:
#   1. A local URL must be loopback: 127.0.0.1, localhost, ::1 or [::1]. Nothing else counts.
#   2. A local key must be a local demo key (its JWT `iss` claim is "supabase-demo"). The
#      hosted publishable key must never be put in these two variables, and a local demo key
#      must never be put in the two above - either mix is refused.
#   3. Setting only one half of either pair is refused, rather than completing it from the
#      other pair.
#   4. The mode ("local" or "hosted") is derived from the validated host. There is no mode
#      variable to set, and no second place for the answer to disagree with itself.
#   5. A URL must be an absolute http(s) URL with no path. A trailing slash is ignored.
#
# The names are the ones the local test tooling already uses (supabase/tests/*), so a local
# run needs no separate configuration file.
SOMAMAP_LOCAL_SUPABASE_URL=
SOMAMAP_LOCAL_ANON_KEY=
#
# Server-side only. Never prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_: it must not reach the browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
META_API_KEY=

